  "worked_solution": "We notice that $Y$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix and $U$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $Y$ and $3$ rows in $U.$ Since the number of columns in $Y$ equals the number of rows in $U,$ the matrices $Y$ and $U$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $YU$ has dimensions $1\\times 1:$\n\n$$\n{Y}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{U}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 1}={YU}_{1\\times 1}\n$$",
